From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:20:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] backends/edid: Set the unusable chromaticity status without a
 split ternary

The project style checker re-indents the continued conditional
expression. Choose the status with an if statement instead; no
behaviour changes. The upstream-facing series carries this in the
commit that added it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
---
 src/backends/edid-parse.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/edid-parse.c b/src/backends/edid-parse.c
index c58a6a2..f4ee9d8 100644
--- a/src/backends/edid-parse.c
+++ b/src/backends/edid-parse.c
@@ -273,8 +273,10 @@ read_native_chromaticities (MetaEdidInfo         *info,
 
   if (unsupported || conflict)
     {
-      info->native_chromaticities_status = unsupported ?
-        META_NATIVE_CHROMATICITIES_UNSUPPORTED : META_NATIVE_CHROMATICITIES_CONFLICT;
+      if (unsupported)
+        info->native_chromaticities_status = META_NATIVE_CHROMATICITIES_UNSUPPORTED;
+      else
+        info->native_chromaticities_status = META_NATIVE_CHROMATICITIES_CONFLICT;
       memset (&info->native_chromaticities, 0, sizeof (info->native_chromaticities));
       return;
     }
